# A1-T01, C2-S01 to C2-S03 — the road, Iron on the Horizon, the Knight-Commander,
# Ironhold Gate. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2078–2204.
# Scene: scenes/chapter2/ironhold_gate.tscn (cinematic).
# Source fix: Kaelen recognises Seraphina's VOICE (her cabin cadence), not her
# face. He never really looked at the crew. That's why she has to test him.

~ road
Elara: You keep checking the sky.
Kaelen: Habit.
Elara: Bad sky where you're from?
Kaelen: Less programmable, usually.
Elara: And what's an airplane, anyway? You keep nearly saying it.
Kaelen: A metal tube that talks gravity into waiting.
Elara: Not very well, then.
do kaelen_stops
# He stops walking. She hears what she just said.
Elara: ...Sorry.
Kaelen: No. You're not wrong.
do walk_on

# C2-S01 — Iron on the Horizon.
~ horizon
do ironhold_reveal
Kaelen (Internal): Workshops at the bottom. Market terraces on top of those. Fortress bridges right at the top, and a clock tower you can see from anywhere, like it wants you to know the time.
Elara: Try not to insult anyone before we find a bed.
Kaelen: I did fine in Oakhaven.
Elara: Mara charged you double.
Kaelen: That was personal.
Elara: It got personal very quickly.
do convoy_passes
Paladin: Left side clear! Keep the centre open! Children stay inside the wagons!
Kaelen (Internal): Keep the aisle clear...
[if elara_trust_high] Elara: Kaelen?
[if not elara_trust_high] Elara: Stranger?
Kaelen: I know that voice.

# C2-S02 — The Knight-Commander.
~ commander
do seraphina_helmet_off
Seraphina: Move, please. You're standing in the lane.
Kaelen: I know you.
Seraphina: That line works better without a sword on your hip.
Kaelen: Your voice. You said "keep the aisle clear".
Kaelen: Flight 707.
do seraphina_grip
Seraphina: Where did you hear that number?
Kaelen: I was on it.
do pause 1.2
Seraphina: What seat?
Kaelen: What?
Seraphina: Your seat. What was it?
Kaelen: I don't remember.
Seraphina: Row?
Kaelen: I don't—
Seraphina: Window or aisle?
Kaelen: ...Window.
# Her breath catches. She was working the right-hand side that day.
Seraphina: You were there.
Elara: You two know each other?
Seraphina: No.
do pause 0.8
Seraphina: We died together.
do kaelen_still
# She regrets it the moment it's out.
Seraphina: Or nearly. Nearly died.
Kaelen: That's a big correction.
Seraphina: I've had practice making it.
set ch2_seraphina_met

# C2-S03 — Ironhold Gate. Three queues: residents, traders, Fracture inspection.
~ gate
Gate Officer: Knight-Commander.
Kaelen: Knight-Commander?
Seraphina: Later.
Kaelen: You were a flight attendant.
Seraphina: Later.
Elara: I like her.
Seraphina: You can stop liking me after the paperwork. They're with me, officer. Inspection line, then residents.
do queues
Rook: That crate is medicinal resin.
Clerk: It's listed as decorative sap.
Rook: Because whoever wrote that category has never been ill in their life.
# He notices Kaelen. He doesn't introduce himself. He files him away.
Kaelen (Internal): That man just looked at me the way Bran looks at a ledger.
set ch2_ironhold_entered
